#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""
Bayesian Artist Ranking System for NovelAI Image Generation

A blind comparison system that generates images with solo, duo, and trio artist
combinations and learns a global Bayesian pairwise-preference ranking. Matchmaking
selects globally by expected information value; the 150-person working set is only a cache.

Modified version:
- Maintains a configurable rolling buffer of 1-50 ready comparisons (default: 5)
- Generates replacement comparisons sequentially in a background worker
- Lets the user vote through already-generated comparisons without waiting
- Supports voting by clicking either image
- Exposes the app on the local network for phone access
- Adds a phone-only Compare layout with Image A above Image B and touch-sized controls
- Restores resilient vote sounds on desktop and phone with browser-audio unlocking and fallback playback
- Adds reliable phone-only buttons for revealing artist tags and duel type
- Adds a persistent phone-only compact image mode that hides redundant labels and Pick Image buttons
- Supports persistent saved prompt presets containing complete positive and negative prompts
- Supports random per-duel prompt rotation that replaces the full prompt with one selected saved preset
- Preserves existing ELO/history/active-pool storage files
- Stores comparison images in D:\\Storage\\Programs\\ArtistEloImages
- Adds an automatic 80%-coverage selection taper plus a persisted manual Selection mode
- Cleans the 25 oldest app-specific Gradio temp entries every 50 generated images
- Uses the same random seed for both sides of every duel
- Tracks separate solo, duo, and trio artist ELO ratings
- Tracks whole artist-combination ELO ratings
- Persists the ready-duel buffer across restarts
- Creates automatic rolling backups every 50 rated duels
- Uses balanced close-rating, discovery, and newcomer-challenge matchmaking
- Penalizes recent repeat matchups and overexposed artists
- Accelerates newcomer evaluation and rotates weak newcomers out sooner
- Tracks confidence-aware, opponent-strength-weighted win rates and treats artists present on both sides as neutral
- Records and reveals the reason each matchup was selected
- Uses a tabbed Phase 3 interface with dedicated Artists and Combinations browsers
- Supports searching, filtering, and sorting by ELO, win rate, weighted win rate, duels, and name
- Replaces cryptic leaderboard abbreviations with clear labels and an explanatory legend
- Lazily loads and caches browser data to prevent tab freezes
- Uses small server-side paginated tables instead of rendering the full ranking set
- Limits the polling timer to lightweight comparison-state updates
- Adds lazy paginated duel history with cached thumbnails and full-resolution opt-in
- Adds favorites for artists, combinations, images, and complete duels with tags and notes
- Adds a lazy Favorites browser and favorite-first ranking sorts
- Adds storage dashboards, configurable Gradio cleanup, thumbnail cleanup, and safe orphan scans
- Avoids automatic CSV regeneration after every vote and reuses one shared ranking-statistics cache
- Serves D-drive comparison images directly instead of recopying them to Gradio temp
- Separates persistence scheduling from disk I/O so background saves cannot block votes
- Adds automatic rank/status badges and independent removable manual tags for artists and combinations
- Adds Undefeated and Battle-tested performance badges
- Restores keyboard shortcuts: 1=A, 2=B, S=skip, 0=undo
- Uses linear active-pool replacement selection for instant rotation votes
- Exposes manual artist/combination tags in Compare and Gallery / Duels
- Allows correcting historical Gallery duel winners and chronologically rebuilding ratings
- Adds transient pause/resume generation that finishes the in-progress duel before stopping
- Replaces large per-tab favorite/tag editors with contextual image/name actions
- Adds direct artist and combination navigation between ranking and Gallery tabs
- Compacts Compare status and reorganizes explanatory UI into collapsed guides
- Adds dense side rankings, bounded Gallery/Favorites tables, and compact navigation controls
- Adds P/L keyboard shortcuts for generation pause and leaderboard visibility
- Adds persistent swapping between the Results and Top Artists panels on Compare
- Refreshes only the ranking/history views affected by each contextual action
- Lets the Artists search match automatic and manual category names
- Uses theme-aware category badge colors for light and dark themes
- Adds contextual private notes for artists and exact combinations across all non-storage tabs
- Adds a coverage-first discovery phase with unseen-artist pool reservation and fresh-vs-fresh screening
- Replaces prose-heavy duel results with responsive outcome, side, metric, and rotation cards
- Replaces the fragile Gallery Dataframe DOM enhancement with a dedicated accessible HTML duel list
- Adds a Both bad vote: legacy/combination tie plus absolute poor-output reliability evidence, without relative skill evidence
- Enforces a strict configured active-pool cap with one-for-one fresh-screening admission
- Renders the virtual Gallery artist list in a body-level floating layer to prevent clipping
- Adds Gallery artist-token versus queries using a single VS separator
- Adds correction and Favorites actions directly to the Gallery duel pop-up
- Adds a right-click Copy name action that copies NovelAI artist emphasis syntax
- Slightly enlarges artist portraits and scales them further as Artist-table column groups are collapsed
- Treats current and queued buffer duels as provisional exposure to prevent duplicate bursts
- Enforces phase quotas across the rolling buffer and keeps unseen artists exclusive to solo fresh screenings
- Fully seeds the 45% unseen reserve at startup/rebuild so fresh screenings do not wait for completed votes
- Restores server-backed clickable sorting headers for Artists and Combinations with active ▲/▼ indicators
- Hard-reserves every artist already present in the rolling buffer to prevent duplicate bursts
- Restricts Fresh discovery to one solo unseen-vs-unseen opening per artist
- Counts Fresh discovery at 50% weight in the solo/duo/trio quota to prevent early duo/trio overcompensation
- Integrates config.py palettes directly into Gradio Settings → Appearance with native Light/Dark bases
- Seeds a removable pink New List tag for artists imported from the Top-2,000 audit
- Revalidates matchmaking stages before every selection so generated labels cannot remain stale
"""

